            <ArticleTitle>Bio-electrical brain relations of pain and acupuncture effects on EEG spectral analysis in healthy volunteers.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>199-205</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Pain description and objective evaluation is difficult. In the last few years, a number of neuro-physiological methods have been used in the study of pain and acupuncture analgesia. EEG spectral analysis allows the description and objective quantification of brain bio-electrical activity changes. The present study aims at evaluating ischemic experimental pain, electroacupuncture (EA) and ischemic pain following EA on EEG spectral analysis in healthy volunteers.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
